# The Certification Gap

Code and data for *The Certification Gap: An Identity-Based Critic Quality
Diagnostic for Deep Reinforcement Learning* (NeurIPS 2026 D&B, under
submission). See `paper.pdf` for the manuscript.

The paper shows empirically that **the Bellman residual `ε_u` — the
canonical critic-quality scalar logged by every PPO/SAC implementation we
surveyed — is uninformative as a per-update predictor of policy harm**
(AUROC 0.45 across 8 environments × 20 seeds, at chance), and that an
algebraic decomposition of the policy improvement
(`J(π_{k+1}) − J(π_k) = A_k − Δ̂_k`) yields a metric whose start-state-bias
component `Δ̂_k` is informative (AUROC 0.68 pooled, dominates `ε_u` in
158 of 159 paired seeds, p < 10⁻²⁷).

## Layout

```
paper.pdf                    # the manuscript
DATASHEET.md                 # Gebru-style data sheet for the released benchmark
REPRODUCIBILITY.md           # NeurIPS reproducibility checklist
LICENSE                      # MIT
pyproject.toml               # dependency pinning
Makefile                     # one-command targets

certgap/                     # the python package
├── common/                  # configs, networks, rollouts, GAE, metrics, env utils
├── tabular/                 # exact-DP RandomMDP + REINFORCE; identity verification
├── geometry/                # policy Jacobian + certified-ratio analysis
├── ppo.py                   # single train_ppo() with paper-aligned per-update logging
├── runners/
│   ├── run_one.py           # single (env, seed, hp_cell) launcher
│   └── sweep.py             # multiprocess pool over a grid spec
└── analysis/
    ├── harm_prediction.py   # AUROC, AUPRC, calibration deciles, bootstrap CIs
    ├── correlations.py      # Pearson / Spearman / paired Wilcoxon (Fisher-z CIs)
    ├── factorial.py         # hyperparameter heatmap aggregation
    └── estimator_agreement.py  # train vs held-out Δ̂ regression

figures/                     # one script per paper figure → PDF in figures/out/
├── fig1_auroc_bars.py
├── fig2_calibration.py
├── fig3_factorial.py
├── fig4_concurrent_vs_lag1.py
├── fig5_pooled_scatter.py
└── appendix/
    ├── figA1_tabular_identity.py
    ├── figA2_decomposition.py
    ├── figA3_eps_u_variants.py
    ├── figA4_lag1_autocorrelation.py
    └── figA5_trajectory.py

results/                     # released benchmark dataset (~70k labeled examples)
├── main/                    # 8 envs × 20 seeds = 160 PPO runs
├── factorial_lunarlander/   # 16 cells × 5–20 seeds
├── factorial_halfcheetah/   # 9 cells × 5–20 seeds
├── factorial_hopper/        # 9 cells × 5 seeds
├── eps_u_variants/          # 6 seeds, Humanoid (logs three ε_u definitions)
├── heldout_humanoid/        # 20 seeds, Humanoid (logs train + held-out Δ̂)
└── tabular/                 # 24 NPG-on-RandomMDP CSVs (identity verification)

scripts/
├── run_all.py               # master runner (every sweep, --skip-if-exists)
├── build_table1.py          # compiles paper Table 1 from results/main/
├── analyze_preliminary.py   # quick overview of every sweep's headline numbers
└── run_*.sh                 # individual entry points per sweep

tests/                       # pytest smoke tests
slop(ARCHIVE,IGNORE)/        # frozen exploration archive — not used by paper
```

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv/bin/pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

MuJoCo experiments require `gymnasium[mujoco]>=1.0` and `mujoco>=3.0`; the
install line pulls both.

## Reproducing the paper

**One command, regenerate every figure and the table from cached results:**

```bash
make figures
.venv/bin/python -m scripts.build_table1
```

That produces 5 main + 5 appendix PDFs in `figures/out/`, plus
`figures/out/table1.tex`. Total time: under two minutes on a laptop.

**One command, full pipeline from scratch (≈13 wall hours at 6 workers):**

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/run_all.py --workers 6 --skip-if-exists
```

`--skip-if-exists` makes this idempotent — if every pickle is already on
disk, it's a no-op.

**Smoke test (~5 minutes, no MuJoCo needed):**

```bash
make verify
```

## Reproducing individual sweeps

| Paper section | Sweep | Command |
|---|---|---|
| §3 main grid | 8 envs × 20 seeds | `bash scripts/run_main_discrete.sh && bash scripts/run_main_mujoco.sh` |
| §4.3 LL factorial | 4×4 × 5 seeds | `bash scripts/run_factorial_lunarlander.sh` |
| §4.3 HC factorial | 3×2 + vlr × 5 seeds | `bash scripts/run_factorial_halfcheetah.sh` |
| §4.3 Hopper factorial | 3×2 + vlr × 5 seeds | `bash scripts/run_factorial_hopper.sh` |
| §4.3 estimator agreement | Humanoid × 20 seeds with held-out logging | `bash scripts/run_heldout_humanoid.sh` |
| §4.1 ε_u variants | Humanoid × 6 seeds with all three ε_u definitions | `bash scripts/run_eps_u_variants.sh` |
| Appendix A1 tabular | 3 RandomMDP families × 8 seeds | `bash scripts/run_tabular.sh` |

